# w.request: a reusable world: the meaning of one request a person makes of an application (owner's GO, reviewer
# block 2026-11-15 14:00, item 1). A request has an act (a k.actions act: make, change, remove, place ...), a target
# (a kind of the open world, a thing present in it, or the last result) and constraints, each a fact: a kind wanted or
# not wanted, a count (a number, a range or a named amount of k.expect), a size or extent on the scale of k.expect, an
# attribute with its value, a place, a manner, parts it is to have (with), a topic (about), a length. Every content
# word of the message ends in a constraint (its `words`) or in an `unread` fact: nothing is silently dropped. A reader
# fills one live instance per turn; w.dialogue keeps the requests of a session and revises them; the open tab's world
# receives the request as a goal and its planner fills what was not said from k.expect.
# Declared as data in the library's std.schema format; the acts of std.acts drive it; it has no rule and no function.
# sources: hand-core 1 (hand-written in this repository; own)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: none (hand-written)
# needs: sopworld with std.schema and std.acts (tools/sopworld/VERSION)

@w.request core.module name=w.request version=1 exports=request exports=target exports=constraint exports=intent exports=unread exports=context exports=previous exports=clock exports=lookup exports=filler core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.world std.schema.world name=w.request doc="the meaning of one request: an act, a target and constraints" core.source="hand-core 1"

# A request. `act` the k.actions act (make, change, remove, place, group, connect, ...); `mode` the frame's mode where
# it has one (more, apart). `target` what it acts on: a kind name (circle, pond, story), a thing of the live world by
# its id, or the last result; `refers` says which (kind, thing, last). `goes_to` the world it goes to (the open tab's
# world: w.diagram, a drawing, w.document ...). `text` the message as read (English; a message in another language is
# translated at the boundary, `said` keeps the original). `n` the turn it was said at, from 1. `revises` the earlier
# request this one revises (a reaction or "my expectation was ..."): the revision carries the whole new constraint set.
# `status`: open (not done yet), done, partly (some constraint not honoured), refused, replaced (revised by a later one).
# What a reader reads off the message (the names of the library's request contract std.request): `mood` do (an order),
# ask (a question), check (a yes/no check: "is the sun yellow?"), propose (a suggestion: "what about a red roof?");
# `words` the stretch of the message this request was read from (a message with two requests has two); `words_origin`
# hull: `words` was not marked but taken as the stretch from the first to the last word of the request's parts;
# `predicate` the verb or phrase that says the act, as written ("thicken", "get rid of"); `question` the kind of
# question of mood ask or check (count, exists, list, what, which, describe, total ...), `asked` the key asked about
# ("what colour is the sun?": drawn.colour).
# A reader's act bank can be finer than k.actions: `mode` then names the narrower act inside the k.actions act, the way
# w.lang.en's mode_map reads "take the group apart" as group in the mode apart. The narrower acts and their act, each
# what a k.actions verb of the same name means: place mode=arrange (lay several things out among themselves: a grid,
# a row, even gaps, aligned); group mode=merge (several things become one); take apart mode=ungroup (a group is
# dissolved, its members stay), mode=split (one thing becomes several), mode=disconnect (the line or join between two
# things is taken away); change mode=reverse (the order or the direction turned round), mode=set (a value made the
# standing default for what is made later: "from now on make the charts detailed"); copy mode=repeat (the last act
# done again, on the same or another thing).
@w.request.request core.type of=w.request.request extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.act core.slot of=w.request.request key=act required=true kind=atom kind=string type=k.actions.act by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.mode core.slot of=w.request.request key=mode kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.target core.slot of=w.request.request key=target kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.refers core.slot of=w.request.request key=refers enum=kind enum=thing enum=last enum=world default=kind core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.goes_to core.slot of=w.request.request key=goes_to kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.text core.slot of=w.request.request key=text kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.said core.slot of=w.request.request key=said kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.n core.slot of=w.request.request key=n kind=integer min=1 step=1 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.revises core.slot of=w.request.request key=revises type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.status core.slot of=w.request.request key=status enum=open enum=done enum=partly enum=refused enum=replaced default=open core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.mood core.slot of=w.request.request key=mood enum=do enum=ask enum=check enum=propose core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.words core.slot of=w.request.request key=words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.words_origin core.slot of=w.request.request key=words_origin enum=hull core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.predicate core.slot of=w.request.request key=predicate kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.question core.slot of=w.request.request key=question enum=count enum=exists enum=list enum=what enum=which enum=where enum=when enum=who enum=describe enum=why enum=how enum=how_much enum=compare enum=total enum=average enum=max enum=min enum=difference enum=percent core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.request.asked core.slot of=w.request.request key=asked kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
# `asked_words` the words of the message that name the key asked about ("what colour is it").
@w.request.request.asked_words core.slot of=w.request.request key=asked_words many=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# The target of a request as the reader read it (std.request.target): one fact per request. `family` the family of
# things of the open tab it is (drawn, node, link, chart, meeting, part, face, text, page ...); `mode` new (made by the
# request), existing (a thing already there), bound (the thing an earlier request made or named); `determiner` as
# written: definite, indefinite, quantified ("all the boxes"), possessive ("her hair"), demonstrative ("this box"); a
# mention read two ways keeps both, the reader's own first. `fill` says how an existing target is given: written (by
# its name), context (by what is on the page or was said last), description (a kind and words: "the big house"), all
# (every thing of the kind), journal_step (a step of the history: "the last change"). `sort` the canonical kind and
# `sort_words` the words that said it (`sort`, as in the other worlds: `kind` is the thing's own type in std.schema);
# `name` the name as written; `description` the words that describe it;
# `count_words` and `count` how many; `quantifier` the quantifier as written (all, every, both, each, "one by one");
# `quantity` the amount word the reader normalised it to (one, two, some, both); `ordinal` which one by order
# (first, last, second_last, newest, leftmost, "first two"); `code_words` the words that gave a code; `ids` the codes
# of the things it names (n1, e2; many). `present=true`: a fact without that key is refused when told (`required` is
# a key a host may still ask for), here and in the kinds below.
@w.request.target core.type of=w.request.target extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.request core.slot of=w.request.target key=request required=true present=true type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.family core.slot of=w.request.target key=family required=true present=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.mode core.slot of=w.request.target key=mode required=true present=true enum=new enum=existing enum=bound core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.determiner core.slot of=w.request.target key=determiner many=true enum=definite enum=indefinite enum=quantified enum=possessive enum=demonstrative core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.fill core.slot of=w.request.target key=fill enum=written enum=context enum=description enum=all enum=journal_step core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.sort core.slot of=w.request.target key=sort kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.sort_words core.slot of=w.request.target key=sort_words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.name core.slot of=w.request.target key=name kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.description core.slot of=w.request.target key=description kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.count_words core.slot of=w.request.target key=count_words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.count core.slot of=w.request.target key=count kind=integer min=0 step=1 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.quantifier core.slot of=w.request.target key=quantifier kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.quantity core.slot of=w.request.target key=quantity kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.ordinal core.slot of=w.request.target key=ordinal kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.code_words core.slot of=w.request.target key=code_words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.target.ids core.slot of=w.request.target key=ids many=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
# `thing` the object of the page (a w.request.context wire of the same request graph) the target is, when the message names it.
@w.request.target.thing core.slot of=w.request.target key=thing many=true type=w.request.context core.source="hand-core 1"
# `family_words` the words of the message that name the target's family ("the chart", "my face") when no kind is said.
@w.request.target.family_words core.slot of=w.request.target key=family_words many=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
# `name_words` the words of the message that introduce the target's name ("a box called Start", "labelled Review").
@w.request.target.name_words core.slot of=w.request.target key=name_words many=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# A constraint of a request: one thing the person said (or the planner assumed) about the result. `on` says what it
# constrains:
#   kind      a kind of thing in the result (`value` the kind: circle, duck, house)
#   count     how many (`number`, or `min`/`max`, or `amount` a k.expect amount: few, several, many), of `of` when given
#   size      the size of each thing (`value` a k.expect scale step: tiny, small, default, big, huge)
#   extent    how much of the canvas or page the result takes (`value` a scale step; `place` narrows it: in a corner)
#   attribute an attribute of the things (`attribute` a k.attributes name: colour; `value` its value: red)
#   place     where (`relation` in, on, at, next_to ...; `value` the place: corner, left, top, centre, or a thing)
#   manner    how (`value`: nice, better, tidy, random, logical, simple, colourful, symmetric)
#   layout    the arrangement (`value` a k.layouts layout or a k.diagrams layout: grid, radial, top_down, circle)
#   with      parts it is to have (`value` the part kind: arrow, water plant, duck; `count` facts may name it in `of`)
#   about     a topic (`value` the topic in words: the water cycle, a dragon)
#   length    how long a text is (`number` or `min`/`max` or `amount`, in `unit`: word, sentence, paragraph, chapter, page)
# `want`: yes (wanted, the default), no (not wanted: "not a circle", "without arrows", "instead of circles"), not_all
# ("not all circles": the kind may appear, but not as every thing: the result has more than one kind). `of` the kind
# the constraint is about where it is not the target ("red circles": attribute colour red of circle). `words` the words
# of the message it was read from (every content word is in one constraint or in an unread fact). `origin`: said (by
# the person), default (filled by the planner from k.expect: an assumption the reply names), reaction (added by a
# reaction of w.dialogue to the last result). `honoured`: what the world did with it (yes, no, partly), set after the
# plan; `why` says why not, in words, for the reply.
# What a reader reads (std.request.constraint): `attribute` may be a key of the open tab's family (drawn.colour,
# chart.labels, meeting.time); `value` is one value or several (a chart's values 30, 25, 20: many); `operator` eq (is
# that value), degree (a step of a scale: big, tiny), delta (more or less than now, by `step`: more, much_more, less,
# much_less), factor (times as much), relation (a place relation to a landmark: left_of, near), region (a region of
# the page: top, corner), less.equal and greater.equal (at most, at least); `phase` selector (it picks the target:
# "the red box") or result (what the request is to bring about); `character` requirement (default) or preference
# ("ideally blue"); `measure` an amount said with a unit (`unit`: minute, pixel, word ...) and `measure_words` the
# words that said it; `open_value` true: the value is outside the reader's bank of values for that key and keeps the
# words as written.
@w.request.constraint core.type of=w.request.constraint extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.request core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=request required=true type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.on core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=on required=true enum=kind enum=count enum=size enum=extent enum=attribute enum=place enum=manner enum=layout enum=with enum=about enum=length core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.want core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=want enum=yes enum=no enum=not_all default=yes core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.value core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=value many=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.of core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=of kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.attribute core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=attribute kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.relation core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=relation kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.number core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=number kind=number min=0 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.min core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=min kind=number min=0 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.max core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=max kind=number min=0 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.amount core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=amount kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.unit core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=unit kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.words core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.origin core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=origin enum=said enum=default enum=reaction default=said core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.honoured core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=honoured enum=yes enum=no enum=partly core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.why core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=why kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.operator core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=operator enum=eq enum=degree enum=delta enum=factor enum=relation enum=region enum=less.equal enum=greater.equal core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.phase core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=phase enum=selector enum=result default=result core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.character core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=character enum=requirement enum=preference default=requirement core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.step core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=step enum=more enum=much_more enum=less enum=much_less core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.measure core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=measure kind=number min=0 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.measure_words core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=measure_words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.constraint.open_value core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=open_value kind=boolean core.source="hand-core 1"
# `thing` the object of the page the constraint names (the anchor of a relation, the node a link goes to), when the message names it.
@w.request.constraint.thing core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=thing many=true type=w.request.context core.source="hand-core 1"
# `key_words` the words of the message that name the key ("the colour", "the x axis", "facing"), beside `words` (the value's words).
@w.request.constraint.key_words core.slot of=w.request.constraint key=key_words many=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# What the result of a request is for and where it goes, as repeated facts owned by the request (the coordinator's
# INTEGRATE-3 contract): an intent is not a target and not a constraint, so it never replaces either. `request` the
# request it belongs to (the owner, a typed reference); `role` purpose (why the result is wanted: "for the board", "to
# compare the regions") or destination (where it goes: "in the quarterly report", "to the appendix"); `value` the value
# of the role in words; `words` the exact words of the message the intent was read from; `want` yes (wanted, the
# default) or no (not wanted: "not for social media"). A request has any number of intents, in any order; the same role
# may repeat. A wire with no owner, or with an owner that is not a request, is refused by the schema and by the dataset
# codec, never silently attached by proximity or by a name.
@w.request.intent core.type of=w.request.intent extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.intent.request core.slot of=w.request.intent key=request type=w.request.request required=true present=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.intent.role core.slot of=w.request.intent key=role enum=purpose enum=destination required=true present=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.intent.value core.slot of=w.request.intent key=value kind=string required=true present=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.intent.words core.slot of=w.request.intent key=words kind=string required=true present=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.intent.want core.slot of=w.request.intent key=want enum=yes enum=no default=yes core.source="hand-core 1"

# A content word of the message that no constraint took (P5: the reply names it). `text` the word or words, `n` its
# place in the message (from 1), `note` what the reader guessed, if anything: a meaning with no key yet (the frame:
# page.time, chart.aggregation), and `value` its value or values as read (many).
@w.request.unread core.type of=w.request.unread extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.unread.request core.slot of=w.request.unread key=request required=true type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.unread.text core.slot of=w.request.unread key=text required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.unread.n core.slot of=w.request.unread key=n kind=integer min=1 step=1 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.unread.note core.slot of=w.request.unread key=note kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.unread.value core.slot of=w.request.unread key=value many=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# What the reader saw when it read the message (its context). `context`: a thing on the page of the open tab: its
# `sort` (its kind: house, box, meeting), `name`, `code` (n1, e2), `size` (a scale step: tiny, small, medium, big,
# huge), `y` (top, bottom) and `text`. `previous`: the message before this one (`text`). `clock`: the time the message
# was read (`now`, a date and time) in `timezone`.
@w.request.context core.type of=w.request.context extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.sort core.slot of=w.request.context key=sort required=true present=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.name core.slot of=w.request.context key=name kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.code core.slot of=w.request.context key=code kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.size core.slot of=w.request.context key=size kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.y core.slot of=w.request.context key=y kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.context.text core.slot of=w.request.context key=text kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.previous core.type of=w.request.previous extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.previous.text core.slot of=w.request.previous key=text required=true present=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.clock core.type of=w.request.clock extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.clock.now core.slot of=w.request.clock key=now required=true present=true kind=time.datetime core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.clock.timezone core.slot of=w.request.clock key=timezone required=true present=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# A lookup: something the request needs that the message does not say, to be found in the context. A fact cannot hold a
# variable, so the request says what is missing with this wire, and the host turns it into a question on its context
# (the page, the previous turns, the preferences): e.g. `key=thing` on a target becomes ask('@x <the area's thing type>')
# over the things of the page, and a single match (or the selection, or the last thing made) completes the target.
# `target` or `constraint` names the wire it completes; `key` what is missing: thing (which existing thing "it", "that
# one" is), family (what sort of thing the target is), sort (its kind), value (the value of the constraint), name;
# `from` where to look first: page, previous (the previous turns), preference, or any (the default).
# `key=answer from=request` declares a dependency on the answer to an earlier ask in the same message.
# `antecedent` names that ask and `words` preserves the answer reference as written. An answer from a
# previous message uses `key=answer from=previous` and has no local antecedent. The answer is an input to
# the request, independent of any lookup that identifies its target.
@w.request.lookup core.type of=w.request.lookup extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.request core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=request required=true present=true type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.target core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=target type=w.request.target core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.constraint core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=constraint type=w.request.constraint core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.key core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=key required=true present=true enum=thing enum=family enum=sort enum=value enum=name enum=answer core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.from core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=from enum=page enum=previous enum=preference enum=any enum=request default=any core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.antecedent core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=antecedent type=w.request.request core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.lookup.words core.slot of=w.request.lookup key=words kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# Filler: words of the message that carry no part of a request (a greeting, politeness, a hedge, thanks, a wrapper such
# as "could you"). Every word of the message is evidence of a wire (a request's predicate or words, a target's words, a
# constraint's words, an unread text) or filler: no word is dropped silently. `text` the words as written.
@w.request.filler core.type of=w.request.filler extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.filler.text core.slot of=w.request.filler key=text required=true present=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# A reader key: what a constraint's `attribute=` may name, per tab. `tab` the area whose reader writes it (drawing,
# diagram, document, calendar); `family` the target family it belongs to (page, drawn, chart, node …); `name` the key as
# written in a constraint (family.key: "page.time"); `head` how its value is read (class: a closed list in `value`;
# candidate: a list a value may leave with open_value=true; span: the words; number; joined with + when several apply,
# "class+step"); `value` the values of its list; `about` what it means, with an example; `means` the domain slot it
# fills when one exists (w.drawing.page.time). The keys are in shards/keys.sop; a constraint with an attribute that is
# no key of its tab is refused by the dataset checker.
@w.request.key core.type of=w.request.key extends=std.schema.thing closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.tab core.slot of=w.request.key key=tab required=true enum=drawing enum=diagram enum=document enum=calendar core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.family core.slot of=w.request.key key=family required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.name core.slot of=w.request.key key=name required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.head core.slot of=w.request.key key=head required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.value core.slot of=w.request.key key=value many=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.about core.slot of=w.request.key key=about kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.key.means core.slot of=w.request.key key=means kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# The kinds and the acts that apply to them. A session holds at most 500 requests (and their 500 targets) and 2,000
# things of context.
@w.request.kind.request std.schema.kind of=w.request.request world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=change acts=ask acts=copy core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.target std.schema.kind of=w.request.target world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=change acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.constraint std.schema.kind of=w.request.constraint world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=change acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.unread std.schema.kind of=w.request.unread world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.context std.schema.kind of=w.request.context world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=change acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.previous std.schema.kind of=w.request.previous world=w.request acts=make acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.clock std.schema.kind of=w.request.clock world=w.request acts=make acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.lookup std.schema.kind of=w.request.lookup world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.filler std.schema.kind of=w.request.filler world=w.request acts=make acts=remove acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.kind.key std.schema.kind of=w.request.key world=w.request acts=ask core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.limit.request std.schema.limit of=w.request.request max=500 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.limit.constraint std.schema.limit of=w.request.constraint max=5000 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.limit.unread std.schema.limit of=w.request.unread max=2000 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.limit.target std.schema.limit of=w.request.target max=500 core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.request.limit.context std.schema.limit of=w.request.context max=2000 core.source="hand-core 1"

# Words: for the world, its kinds and its keys.
